  "issue": {
    "body": "I use pytest in combination with [pytest-asyncio](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest-asyncio), so all of my unit tests are coroutines. Currently I have a fixture that replaces the `TestClient`'s existing `__enter__` and `__exit__` methods to be usable asynchronously directly:\r\n```python\r\n@pytest.fixture\r\nasync def client():\r\n    tc = TestClient(app)\r\n    tc.send_queue = asyncio.Queue()\r\n    tc.receive_queue = asyncio.Queue()\r\n    tc.task = asyncio.create_task(tc.lifespan())\r\n    await tc.wait_startup()\r\n    try:\r\n        yield tc\r\n    finally:\r\n        await tc.wait_shutdown()\r\n```\r\nIt would be nice if the TestClient provided `__aenter__` and `__aexit__` methods to do this automatically as an [async context manager](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0492/#asynchronous-context-managers-and-async-with). I can provide a pull request if you want.",
    "closed_at": "2022-02-08T12:37:40Z",
    "created_at": "2020-06-15T19:44:11Z",
